.TH RATAPLAY 1 "May 2026" "rataplay 1.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rataplay \- Terminal YouTube Search & Play
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rataplay
[\fIquery\fR]
[\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Rataplay
is a high-performance terminal user interface for searching, playing, and
downloading YouTube videos. It uses
.B mpv
for playback and
.B yt\-dlp
for metadata extraction, searching, and downloading.

If a
.I query
is provided on the command line, it is executed as a search on startup.
.I query
can be a search term or a YouTube URL (video, playlist, or channel).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI query
Search query or YouTube URL to open on startup.
.TP
.B \-v , \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h , \-\-help
Print help information and exit.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.SS Navigation
.TP
.B s , /
Focus the search bar (enter editing mode).
.TP
.B j , Down
Move selection down.
.TP
.B k , Up
Move selection up.
.TP
.B Enter
Open action menu for the selected item, or load more search results.
.TP
.B Space
Toggle multi-select on the focused item.
.TP
.B Backspace , b
Go back (pop playlist stack) or close the current panel.
.TP
.B Tab
Switch focus to the downloads panel.
.TP
.B Esc
Go back, close overlay, or exit editing mode.
.TP
.B q
Quit the application.
.SS Playback Control
.TP
.B p
Toggle pause / resume.
.TP
.B x
Stop current playback.
.TP
.B Left
Seek backward 5 seconds.
.TP
.B Right
Seek forward 5 seconds, or play the selected item externally when not in
audio-only mode.
.TP
.B [
Seek backward 30 seconds.
.TP
.B ]
Seek forward 30 seconds.
.SS Action Menu
When the action menu is open on a search result:
.TP
.B w
Watch the video externally in an mpv window.
.TP
.B t
Watch the video in the terminal using mpv with tct output.
.TP
.B a
Listen to audio only (no video).
.TP
.B d
Open the download dialog.
.TP
.B o
Open the video or playlist URL in your default web browser.
.TP
.B c
Copy the video URL or channel ID to the clipboard.
.TP
.B i
Copy the channel ID to clipboard.
.TP
.B p
Open the parent playlist (if the video belongs to one).
.TP
.B l
Download all items in the current playlist or view.
.TP
.B s
Download all multi-selected items.
.SS Settings State
.TP
.B Enter , Right , l
Toggle or edit the selected setting.
.TP
.B Esc , q
Close the settings menu.
.TP
.B j , Down
Move selection down.
.TP
.B k , Up
Move selection up.
.SS Editing Mode
When the search bar or a settings input field is focused:
.TP
.B Enter
Execute search or confirm the setting value.
.TP
.B Esc , Tab
Exit editing mode.
.TP
.B Left
Move cursor one character left.
.TP
.B Right
Move cursor one character right.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Left
Move cursor one word left.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Right
Move cursor one word right.
.TP
.B Home
Move cursor to beginning of line.
.TP
.B End
Move cursor to end of line.
.TP
.B Backspace
Delete character before cursor.
.TP
.B Delete
Delete character at cursor.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Backspace , Ctrl+w , Ctrl+h
Delete word backwards.
.TP
.B Ctrl+u
Delete all text before cursor (clear to start of line).
.TP
.B Ctrl+k
Delete all text after cursor (clear to end of line).
.TP
.B Ctrl+a
Move cursor to beginning of line.
.TP
.B Ctrl+e
Move cursor to end of line.
.SS Control Keys (global)
.TP
.B Ctrl+s
Toggle the settings menu.
.TP
.B Ctrl+t
Cycle through available themes.
.TP
.B Ctrl+a
Cycle through logo animation modes.
.TP
.B Ctrl+l
Toggle the live stream filter (re-searches if results are shown).
.TP
.B Ctrl+p
Toggle the playlist filter (re-searches if results are shown).
.SS Downloads Panel
.TP
.B d
Toggle the downloads panel open and closed.
.TP
.B p
Pause, resume, or restart a download task.
.TP
.B x
Cancel a download task, or remove it from the list if finished.
.TP
.B P (Shift)
Resume or restart all selected downloads.
.TP
.B X (Shift)
Cancel all selected downloads.
.SS Format Selection
.TP
.B j , Down
Next format.
.TP
.B k , Up
Previous format.
.TP
.B Enter
Confirm format choice.
.TP
.B Esc , q
Return to the action menu.
.SH MOUSE SUPPORT
.TP
.B Left click
Select items, activate overlays, focus the search bar, toggle pause on the
playback bar.
.TP
.B Double left click
Open the action menu, confirm format selection or download dialog choices.
.TP
.B Scroll
Scroll through search results, downloads, or format lists.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file is at
.IR ~/.config/rataplay/config.toml .
It is hot-reloaded every 500 ms by polling file modification time.
.SS Root Settings
.TP
.BI theme " (string, default: Default)"
Visual theme. One of: Default, Dracula, Matrix, Cyberpunk, Catppuccin.
.TP
.BI search_limit " (integer, default: 20)"
Number of results per search page or "Load More" action.
.TP
.BI playlist_limit " (integer, default: 15)"
Maximum number of videos to load when opening a playlist.
.TP
.BI download_directory " (string, default: ~/Videos/Rataplay)"
Directory where downloads are saved.
.TP
.BI animation " (string, default: Glitch)"
Logo animation mode. One of: Wave, Breathe, Glitch, Neon, Static.
.TP
.BI show_live " (boolean, default: true)"
Include live streams in search results.
.TP
.BI show_playlists " (boolean, default: true)"
Include playlists in search results.
.TP
.B progress_style
(Default: "\f[CB]\-\fP") Character used to render progress bars.
.SS [search_filter] Section
.TP
.BI enabled " (boolean, default: false)"
Enable date-based filtering of search results.
.TP
.BI unit " (string, default: \"\")"
Time unit for the filter. One of: day, week, month.
.TP
.BI value " (integer, default: 1)"
Filter value in the given unit (e.g. 14 with unit "day" = last 14 days).
.SS [executables] Section
.TP
.BI enabled " (boolean, default: false)"
Master switch for custom binary paths.
.TP
.BI mpv " (path)"
Absolute path to the mpv binary.
.TP
.BI ytdlp " (path)"
Absolute path to the yt-dlp binary.
.TP
.BI ffmpeg " (path)"
Absolute path to the ffmpeg binary.
.TP
.BI js_runtime " (path, alias: deno)"
Absolute path to a JavaScript runtime (e.g. deno).
.SS [cookies] Section
.TP
.BI enabled " (boolean, default: false)"
Enable cookie-based authentication for protected content.
.TP
.BI source.type " (string)"
Cookie source type: off, browser, netscape, or json.
.TP
.BI source.value " (string)"
Browser name (chrome, firefox, edge, safari, opera, vivaldi, brave) or file
path, depending on source type.
.SS [logging] Section
.TP
.BI enabled " (boolean, default: false)"
Enable file logging.
.TP
.BI path " (path)"
Custom log file path. Defaults vary by platform:
.RS
.IP Linux: 3
~/.local/state/rataplay/rataplay.log
.IP macOS: 3
~/Library/Logs/rataplay/rataplay.log
.IP Windows: 3
%LOCALAPPDATA%/rataplay/logs/rataplay.log
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/rataplay/config.toml
Configuration file (hot-reloaded).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/rataplay/rataplay.log
Default log file on Linux.
.TP
.I ~/Videos/Rataplay/
Default download directory.
.TP
.I /tmp/rataplay-mpv-*.sock
mpv IPC socket (created at runtime, cleaned up on exit).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TERM
Used to detect terminal capabilities for image rendering.
.B xterm-kitty
enables native Kitty protocol.
.TP
.B TERM_PROGRAM
Used to detect WezTerm for native image rendering.
.SH RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES
The following programs must be installed and available in PATH (version-checked
on startup):
.TP
.B yt-dlp
YouTube search, metadata, format listing, and download.
.TP
.B mpv
Video and audio playback with IPC remote control.
.PP
Optional dependencies:
.TP
.B ffmpeg
Required by yt-dlp for merging downloaded streams.
.TP
.B deno
JavaScript runtime for yt-dlp extractors.
.SH FEATURES
.TP
.B Playlist Browsing
Open playlists to browse their contents; navigate back with Backspace.
.TP
.B Multi-Select
Select multiple items with Space for bulk download or deletion.
.TP
.B Download Management
Pause, resume, cancel downloads. Real-time progress, speed, and ETA display.
.TP
.B Download Persistence
In-progress downloads are restored on restart by scanning .info.json files.
.TP
.B URL Mode
Paste a YouTube URL to search and play directly.
.TP
.B Terminal Graphics
Native image rendering in Kitty and WezTerm; halfblock fallback for others.
.TP
.B MPRIS Media Controls
Desktop media key integration (Play, Pause, Stop, Next, Previous) via D-Bus.
.TP
.B Clipboard Integration
Copy video URLs and channel IDs to the system clipboard.
.TP
.B Paste Support
Bracketed paste for inserting text into input fields.
.TP
.B Garbage Cleanup
Remove orphaned .part, .ytdl, and .tmp files from the download directory.
.TP
.B Config Hot-Reload
Configuration is re-read every 500 ms; changes apply without restart.
.SH THEMES
Available themes: Default, Dracula, Matrix, Cyberpunk, Catppuccin.
Cycle with Ctrl+t.
.SH ANIMATIONS
Available logo animations: Wave, Breathe, Glitch, Neon, Static.
Cycle with Ctrl+a.
.SH KEY FILE
.IR ~/.config/rataplay/config.toml
is auto-generated with comments on first run. All settings have sensible
defaults.
